  "question": {
    "text": "Two particles having masses <math><mi>m</mi></math> and <math><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></math> are separated by distance <math><mi>l</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The distance of the centre of mass from m is <math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is the distance of point at which gravitational field intensity is zero. Find the value of <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br />\r<br />\r<img height=\"41\" src=\"assets\\qt0058_d46e1a88e9bf.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" width=\"197\" />"
  },
